<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hafrsfjord</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 872</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hafrsfjord was a naval battle in the fjord near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavanger">Stavanger</a> in Rogaland, traditionally dated around 872 but possibly later. According to the sagas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> defeated an alliance of western Norwegian kings there. Norwegian tradition treats the battle as the moment when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> was first united under one king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hafrsfjord.jpg" alt="Battle of Hafrsfjord" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hansen 'Ole Peter' Balling · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ole_Peter_Hansen_Balling_Harald_H%C3%A5rfagre_i_slaget_ved_Hafrsfjord.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
